1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
What has been the biggest cultural shock that you've experienced since coming here.
来到这里之后，你经历过最大的文化冲击是什么？

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,360
Two things especially when the people eat especially related to the food.
两件事，尤其是人们吃饭的时间，特别是与食物有关的事。

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:13,000
And how the people are they are very cold I would say not smiling always kind of grumpy I know like serious face.
还有人们的样子。我觉得他们很冷淡，不笑，总有点不高兴，就是一张严肃的脸。

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,320
Instead in italy you see like everyone smiling happy tall and stuff like that.
而在意大利，你会看到大家笑着，开心地……字幕写作 tall，还有类似的样子。

5
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:24,520
People are grumpy in russia like I am a weird because I'm always smiling and I'm like hey yeah guys let's do something together.
俄罗斯的人也不太爱笑。我算个异类，因为我总笑着说：嘿，大家一起做点什么吧。

6
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:29,600
And like people like why are you so happy today I'm like I because I am today here with you.
别人问你今天怎么这么开心，我就说，因为今天我在这里和你们在一起。

7
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:33,680
So yeah that was the thing that like was really similar and I was like okay I'm fine with it.
所以，这点很相似，我就觉得，好吧，我能接受。

8
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:37,040
So let's talk about some of the similarities that poland and hungary have.
来谈谈波兰和匈牙利的一些相似之处。

9
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:43,280
First we both love complaining I think that's why we get along so well.
首先，我们都爱抱怨。我觉得这就是我们那么合得来的原因。

10
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:51,640
Complaining is the best conversation starter for us is it true that hungarians they love to complain I hear this a lot.
抱怨对我们来说是最好的开场话题。匈牙利人爱抱怨是真的吗？我经常听到这话。

11
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:58,320
It's not like we we like to complain but we say out loud authentically if we don't like something.
不是我们喜欢抱怨，而是不喜欢什么就真实地说出来。

12
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:02,030
Other cultures they don't like like it but they don't want to say it.
其他文化的人也不喜欢，但他们不想说出来。

13
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:04,799
Feel we also really honest if you like something.
字幕在这里有个不清楚的 feel；说话人接着说，喜欢什么时我们也很诚实。

14
00:01:04,799 --> 00:01:13,440
I think it's kind of true but of course people who are open minded who have more opportunities who travel the world they are not that negative.
我觉得有点道理。不过，思想开放、机会更多、到处旅行的人没那么消极。

15
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:21,240
But generally speaking here people who are living in the box they don't have too high salaries and stuff so they are struggling with their problems.
但一般来说，这里那些生活在框框里的人，工资不太高，也在为自己的问题挣扎。

16
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:27,480
I like when people say the truth and when someone's always positive it makes me question like how can you be positive all the time that's not real right.
我喜欢别人说实话。有人总是积极，我会想，你怎么能一直积极？那不真实，对吧？

17
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:34,600
Yeah exactly I think if I go out shopping with my best friend who's hungarian and if I try on a a t shirt or something like.
对，没错。比如我和匈牙利闺蜜购物，试穿一件 T 恤之类的东西。

18
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:38,480
They would be like nah and it's so calming for my nerves.
她会直接说，不怎么样。这反而让我安心。

19
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:42,480
For me it's so much tiring if I talk to someone who's like meating around the bush.
如果跟一个说话绕弯的人聊天，我觉得很累；字幕写作 meating around the bush。

20
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:45,760
I'm like just tell me is it good or bad like let's just move on.
我就会说，直接告诉我好还是坏，接着往下说吧。

21
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:50,160
Americans for example they would ask you how are you we take that question seriously.
比如美国人会问你好吗，我们会认真对待这个问题。

22
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:54,520
So we go deep deep down in our traumas and answering you.
于是我们会深入讲自己的创伤来回答你。

23
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:58,760
I think both of our nations are a bit shy we are not that easy going.
我觉得我们两个民族都有点害羞，不那么随和。

24
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:02,440
But once you break the eyes then it it goes really well.
可一旦打破隔阂，就相处得很好；字幕写作 break the eyes。

25
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:07,080
I think it comes out in service for example when you go into a restaurant in the states.
我觉得服务中也能看出来，比如你去美国一家餐馆。

26
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:09,720
Then they're all over of course because of the tipping as well.
他们会特别热情，当然也与小费有关。

27
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:16,199
But at the same time I kind of feel like here people say like are we are rude no we just like we don't put on any facade.
但我也觉得，这里有人会说：我们粗鲁吗？不是，我们只是不给自己装门面。

28
00:02:16,199 --> 00:02:21,230
Sometimes we are super rude though so we don't do any extra effort to fake something that we are not.
不过，有时我们的确特别粗鲁。我们不额外费力假装自己不是的样子。

29
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:26,400
Does that bother you that people can be sometimes rude yeah it does it does.
有人有时会粗鲁，这会困扰你吗？会，确实会。

30
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:32,600
I think I see it less and less but it can be like come on like pull yourself together a little bit.
我觉得这种情况越来越少，但有时还是想说，拜托，稍微振作、调整一下吧。

31
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:38,119
You can't really see if you just go to a restaurant or to a supermarket you could tell.
字幕先说 you can't really see，接着说：如果去餐馆或超市，你其实能看出来。

32
00:02:38,119 --> 00:02:41,160
If the person who works there if they have a good day or not.
你能看出在那里工作的人今天心情好不好。

33
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:48,880
In thailand or the us I think it's completely different it happens but most of the time there they hide their emotions more.
我觉得泰国或美国很不一样，虽也会发生，但大部分时候他们更会隐藏情绪。

34
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:53,240
Here we don't really the waiters in it are always smiling even they hate you even they hate you they smile.
这里我们不太隐藏。字幕说 it 的地方，服务员总是笑着，即使讨厌你也笑。

35
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:57,800
Here uh they are more uh how say clear that oh we don't like you we don't like the job.
这里的人会更直接一点，说，我们不喜欢你，也不喜欢这份工作。

36
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:05,800
We just do it for doing it so in the bars in the restaurants they are so slow I don't know I think I would be a better bartender sometimes.
我们就只是做这份工作。酒吧、餐馆里动作很慢，有时我觉得我都能当个更好的调酒师。

37
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:10,549
Because they just taking really like 10 minutes for a cocktail or something or in the shop.
他们做一杯鸡尾酒竟要十分钟左右；或者在商店里……

38
00:03:10,559 --> 00:03:16,479
They can start talking with a client in front of you at the casher for 10 minutes and you just wait.
前面的顾客在收银处和店员聊十分钟，你只能等。

39
00:03:16,479 --> 00:03:26,750
But I would say that like new generation is getting better since we are going through a lot of transformations like political economical and everything people are trying to be really kinder to each other.
不过我觉得新一代正在变好。我们经历政治、经济等许多变化，人们也在努力对彼此更友善。
